    "current_semantic_intent": "Use supporting review context followed by a native exception queue and reason codes.",
    "authoritative_narration": "The normal path is only half the design. Missing data, duplicate requests, unusual approvals, and system outages need an explicit destination. Route them to a named owner. Preserve the original input. Avoid silent retries that can create duplicate work. A supporting shot of a team reviewing an exception can make the operational context clear, but the visual remains illustrative. The workflow record is the evidence. Set a threshold for pausing the pilot if exceptions rise. This does not need a complicated control room. A simple queue, a reason code, and a manual fallback can be enough. Control is part of the time-saving design, not a separate concern added later."
  },
